{{!-- What an improvement gives you, in the book's own two halves.

      The book writes every payoff as two sentences — "When you ***meet the requirements***, increase
      Fortunes by 1 and add any new homes to the map. **Henceforth**, when you consume Surplus in
      winter, consider Population to be 1 lower than it is." — and `system.effects` carries that split
      as `trigger.isCompletion`. So: two headed groups, and the HEADING states the trigger so that no
      line has to. Every result appears exactly once, saying only what it does.

      That prose used to sit in the pack as a third statement of the same facts, under the chips and
      the statement lines that already said them, and it was extracted for translation twice over. It
      is gone; this is the only place the payoff is stated now, which is why it renders whether or not
      the improvement is finished. An unearned line is a promise, and carries no control.

      Nothing under **Henceforth** is applied here even where the sheet could write it: those results
      fire at the turn of the season, and the season's own panel is where the table takes them. See
      TurnoverStatement's `stated`.

      Context = an ImprovementPayoff. --}}
<div class="steading-payoff">

	{{#if hasCompletion}}
		<p class="steading-payoff-head">{{rich (localize "stonetop.steading.effects.onCompletion")}}</p>
		{{!-- No source: on an improvement's own card the source IS the card, and gluing it on produced
		      "Additional Housing increase Fortunes by 1". No delta chip either — the chip row on the
		      shut card already states the number, and the line's own words contain it. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.steading-statement" statement=completion showAdvisory=true
		    showAdjustments=true showSource=false showDelta=false}}
	{{/if}}

	{{#if hasHenceforth}}
		<p class="steading-payoff-head">{{rich (localize "stonetop.steading.effects.henceforth")}}</p>
		{{!-- The timing, because "Henceforth" says these fire later without saying when — and the
		      line's own words no longer say it either, since the trigger came out of them with the
		      prose. No delta: the words that remain already contain the number. --}}
		{{!-- showAdjustments: a result that bends a step is part of what this improvement DOES, and the
		      card is the one place that states the whole payoff. The season tab collects them under
		      the step instead; here there is no step to collect them under. --}}
		{{> "stonetop.steading-statement" statement=henceforth showAdvisory=true
		    showAdjustments=true showSource=false showDelta=false showTiming=true}}
	{{/if}}

</div>
